{"author":{"id":"b409816c5cd5ab140d1d52eb33aace35de44952bb794b19806fd57f6ecb1ace9"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1790348155,"nonce":"pRPU2v2LWgQD1fzIwf33Gwyz2UI=","title":"Bytecode major version and snapshot BUILD_ID do not move when the HIR schema changes","message":"The comment at crates/compiler/src/bytecode.rs:567-569 says the major version moves with any layout change, but bd26938 added HirModule.automatic_release under 2.0 without a bump. `#[serde(default)]` on HIR fields (hir.rs:104, :308, :372, :2247-2277; crates/typed_ast/src/source.rs:77) only lets a field be left out in JSON; Postcard and Bincode are positional, so an older file decodes into the wrong fields or fails. The bench runner already works around this with its own CACHE_SCHEMA_VERSION (crates/zynml/benchmarks/bench_runner.rs:55-64).\n\nThe snapshot BUILD_ID hashes only crates/compiler/src (crates/compiler/build.rs:7-26). Span, TypeId, InternedString and ParamOwnership are part of the payload and live in crates/typed_ast, so a change there produces a snapshot whose build id still matches and whose payload does not. 5e24efcb4fb48c15ac0ad0a57dee42ab4308d831fc0a4e8ea988709a4e5bf18f covers refusing a mismatched snapshot; this one is about the mismatch not being detected.\n\nFix: derive the schema identity from the serialized types (hash both crates' sources in build.rs, or a schema fingerprint test that fails when a serialized type changes without a version bump).","files":null}]}